    "result": "## Summary\n\nI successfully fixed all failing tests in the frai-core test suite by identifying and addressing two root causes:\n\n### **Fix 1: Missing named exports (governance.test.js)**\n**Problem**: Test couldn't import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `src/finetune/index.js`\n- Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n### **Fix 2: Incorrect toxicity metric calculation (eval/index.test.js)**\n**Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving `(outputs, references)` but expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, causing references to be treated as banned terms\n- Wrapped the toxicity metric in DEFAULT_METRICS to only pass outputs, ignoring the references parameter\n\n**Result**: All 28 tests now pass across 8 test files. All existing public exports remain functional.",
